Let me check the reka-ui documentation for Menubar content focus behavior.## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
- When the Windows menu opens, **move focus into it** (clicking the trigger opens the menu but leaves focus on the trigger — reka-ui only focuses the first item on *keyboard* opening).
- **Close the menu when focus leaves it** (blur), without breaking the existing toggle-on-trigger click, and without closing when the user clicks non-focusable padding *inside* the panel.

**Strategic Approach**
- Add a `ref` to the trigger and to the content wrapper (the existing `<div class="flex w-[640px] …">`), plus `tabindex="-1"` so the wrapper is programmatically focusable.
- On `openMenu` becoming truthy → `nextTick` → focus the wrapper (skipping if something inside is already focused, e.g. keyboard open).
- Add `@focusout` on the wrapper:
  - keep open if focus stays inside the content,
  - keep open if focus returns to the trigger (it handles its own toggle),
  - keep open if focus drops to `<body>` *and* the press started inside (`pointerDownInside` guard),
  - otherwise close.
- Add `@pointerdown` guard so clicking non-focusable areas inside the panel (padding, section labels, user-info text) doesn't register as a real blur.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `MenubarContent` is portaled; the wrapper div is the single reliable DOM root to attach handlers to.
- Uses `$el ?? element` when resolving component refs (safe for both plain elements and reka-ui components).
- Behaviour is framework-agnostic to the `v-if/v-else` footer swap in `DesktopSidebar.vue`: by the time the avatar is clickable the rail is already floated open, so no remount occurs.

**Target Files**
- `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` (modify)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

1. **`WindowsMenu.vue`** — template: add `ref="menuTrigger"` to `MenubarTrigger`; add `ref`, `tabindex="-1"`, `@focusout`, `@pointerdown` to the content wrapper. Script: add `pointerDownInside` state and `elOf`, `focusMenu`, `onContentPointerDown`, `onFocusOut` methods, plus the focus call in the `openMenu` watcher.

## 3. File changes, Code Block Formatting & Proposed Changes

```vue src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue
<script setup>
import {
  MenubarContent,
  MenubarMenu,
  MenubarPortal,
  MenubarRoot,
  MenubarTrigger,
} from 'reka-ui'
import UserInfoPanel from '../UserInfoPanel.vue'
import WindowsMenuItems from './WindowsMenuItems.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <MenubarRoot v-model="openMenu" :data-theme="$ui.theme">
    <MenubarMenu value="windows-menu" class="MenubarMenu">
      <MenubarTrigger
        ref="menuTrigger"
        class="click select-none outline-none w-full text-left flex items-center"
      >
        <slot />
      </MenubarTrigger>
      <MenubarPortal>
        <MenubarContent
          side="top"
          align="start"
          :side-offset="8"
          :align-offset="0"
          :avoid-collisions="true"
          :data-theme="$ui.theme"
          class="menubar-windows-content relative outline-none p-0 rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 shadow-2xl overflow-hidden bg-base-100 will-change-[transform,opacity]"
        >
          <div
            ref="menuContent"
            tabindex="-1"
            class="flex w-[640px] max-w-[92vw] outline-none"
            @focusout="onFocusOut"
            @pointerdown="onContentPointerDown"
          >
            <!-- LEFT: unified user info panel -->
            <div
              class="w-56 shrink-0 border-r border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/40 p-4 overflow-y-auto max-h-[80vh]"
              @click.stop
            >
              <UserInfoPanel @close="close" />
            </div>

            <!-- RIGHT: apps grid + sections -->
            <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 flex flex-col">
              <WindowsMenuItems @close="close" />

              <!-- Status footer -->
              <div class="mt-auto flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-2 border-t border-base-content/10 text-[11px] text-base-content/60">
                <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span
                    class="inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full"
                    :class="$storex.session.connected ? 'bg-success' : 'bg-error'"
                  ></span>
                  {{ $storex.session.connected ? 'Connected' : 'Offline' }}
                </span>
                <span>codx-junior</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </MenubarContent>
      </MenubarPortal>
    </MenubarMenu>
  </MenubarRoot>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  emits: ['close', 'open'],
  data() {
    return {
      openMenu: '',
      // True while a pointer press started inside the menu content, so losing
      // focus to <body> (clicking non-focusable padding) does not close it.
      pointerDownInside: false
    }
  },
  watch: {
    openMenu(val) {
      if (val) {
        this.focusMenu()
        this.$emit('open')
      } else {
        this.$emit('close')
      }
    }
  },
  methods: {
    // Resolve a template ref to the underlying DOM element
    elOf(ref) {
      return ref?.$el ?? ref ?? null
    },
    // Move focus into the menu when it opens (opening with the pointer does not focus it by default)
    focusMenu() {
      this.$nextTick(() => {
        const content = this.elOf(this.$refs.menuContent)
        if (!content) return
        // Keep whatever is already focused inside the menu (e.g. keyboard-open first item)
        if (content.contains(document.activeElement)) return
        content.focus()
      })
    },
    // Remember presses that start inside the content to distinguish them from real blurs
    onContentPointerDown() {
      this.pointerDownInside = true
      this.$nextTick(() => { this.pointerDownInside = false })
    },
    // Close the menu as soon as focus leaves it
    onFocusOut(event) {
      if (!this.openMenu) return
      const content = this.elOf(this.$refs.menuContent)
      const trigger = this.elOf(this.$refs.menuTrigger)
      const next = event.relatedTarget
      // Focus still inside the menu
      if (next && content?.contains(next)) return
      // Focus returned to the launcher button: it manages its own open/close toggle
      if (next && next === trigger) return
      // Focus dropped to <body>/nothing: keep open when the press started inside
      if (!next && this.pointerDownInside) return
      this.close()
    },
    close() {
      this.openMenu = ''
    }
  }
}
</script>

