## 4. File Change Summary Table

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` | Modify | `MenubarTrigger` | Added `ref="menuTrigger"` so the trigger element can be recognized during `focusout`. |
| `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` | Modify | content wrapper `<div>` | Added `ref="menuContent"`, `tabindex="-1"`, `outline-none`, `@focusout="onFocusOut"`, `@pointerdown="onContentPointerDown"`. |
| `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` | Modify | `data()` | Added `pointerDownInside` flag to distinguish in-panel clicks that blur to `<body>` from real blurs. |
| `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` | Modify | `watch.openMenu` | Calls `focusMenu()` when the menu opens (before emitting `open`). |
| `src/components/main-menu/WindowsMenu.vue` | Modify | `methods` | Added `elOf`, `focusMenu`, `onContentPointerDown`, `onFocusOut`; focus is moved into the menu on open and the menu closes when focus leaves it. |

**Behaviour summary**
- Click the avatar → menu opens **and receives focus** (no change needed for keyboard opens — existing item focus is preserved).
- Click outside, `Tab`/`Esc` away, or focus drops to the page → menu **closes**.
- Clicking non-focusable padding *inside* the panel, or clicking the trigger to toggle it, → menu **stays open / behaves normally**.
